notes: "The materials library is the part I use most. Assets are stored once, at their original size, with their source and usage. This figure is a real one: C1′–C1′ distances at twelve paired positions in PDB 1BNA, one public structure. The plot is this edition's recomputation from its own 2026-11-12 download; the structure is the RCSB assembly image. They are not independent replicates, and not hydrogen-bond distances. The figure is referenced, not re-pasted, so the labels and pixels survive."
